  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nNot much to talk about weather wise over the next week as the \nnortheast remains predominantly under an large upper level \nridge. A noreaster off of the coast today into early Friday is \ngoing to try and take on some tropical characteristics which in \nturn will help strengthen the ridge around the edges of the low \nwhere we are. Temperatures the next couple afternoons were \nbumped up a few degrees with afternoon dew points lowered by \nabout 5 to 10 degrees from models to help lower the RH. With the\nrecent freeze, evapotranspiration has largely ended so its been\neasy the last few days for dew points to get well below \nforecast. Breezy north to northeast winds with the seasonably \nwarm, dry afternoons with the leaves on the ground, fire spread \nwill be elevated through the weekend and likely into early next \nweek as we continue to dry out. \n\nThe only semi interesting thing this week is a trough that \nmoves into New England Friday as the low off the coast departs. \nWith no moisture in place, precipitation is not expected but \ntemperatures will cool slightly for Friday and Saturday before \nwarming up again Sunday into next week.",
